            <ArticleTitle>[A case of choledochal cyst simulating kyphoscoliosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>479-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors describe a patient's case with choledochus cyst whose leading symptom was antalgetic oblique carriage giving rise to the suspicion of kyposcoliosis. They briefly survey the etiopatogenesis, diagnosis and therapy of the choledochus cyst.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
